data_ptbi2
# Phase identity: layered noncentrosymmetric trigonal beta-PtBi2, P31m, Z=3.
# Provenance: Feng et al., Nature Communications 10, 4765 (2019),
# doi:10.1038/s41467-019-12805-2, Supplementary Tables I--II (CC BY 4.0):
# https://www.physics.okayama-u.ac.jp/jeschke_homepage/papers/NatureCommun10p4765_Supplement.pdf
# This P1 basis uses the detailed 273 K cell from SI Table I and expands the
# Pt 3c, Bi1 1a, Bi2 2b, and Bi3 3c coordinates tabulated at 295 K in SI
# Table II. This mixed-temperature use is explicit rather than implying a
# single-temperature refinement. It is the layered trigonal phase, not cubic
# pyrite PtBi2. Layers stack along c and the explicit basis makes 001 finite.
# The catalog B_ang2=0.6 A^2 is a shared modeling placeholder, not either
# displacement parameter reported in the SI.
# Limiting checks: V=sqrt(3)a^2c/2, 3Pt+6Bi, finite basal (001) coupling.
# Validation: ptbi2-p31m-structure
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M 'P 1'
_symmetry_Int_Tables_number 1
_cell_length_a 6.5657
_cell_length_b 6.5657
_cell_length_c 6.1601
_cell_angle_alpha 90.0
_cell_angle_beta 90.0
_cell_angle_gamma 120.0
